From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:41:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Prepare Synapse for deployment on Render + Vercel

- Store uploaded documents in MongoDB GridFS instead of the local disk,
  since Render's filesystem is wiped on every restart and redeploy.
  Older disk-based uploads are still served and deleted correctly.
- Add render.yaml blueprint for the backend (free plan, Singapore,
  health check on /api/health-check, auto-generated JWT_SECRET).
- Add frontend/vercel.json: SPA rewrites so deep links work on refresh,
  and CI=false so CRA lint warnings don't fail the Vercel build.
- Trust the proxy, pin Node >=18, document Atlas/Vercel env values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMuEznxDBR7Eet2DgWfTXw
